---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CTABlock from '../components/CTABlock.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Heurystics"
  description="Pallav Rawat — 8+ years across data, tech, and analytics. Now building and deploying AI systems in the open, one real use case at a time."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
      <h1 class="fade-up">I'm Pallav. Heurystics is my playground for putting AI to work.</h1>
      <p class="lead fade-up delay-1" style="margin-top: 16px;">
        Not a polished agency — a one-person consultancy in practice. Part client work, part
        personal playground, all of it public. I find the boring, manual, repetitive stuff in a
        workflow, then build small AI tools and connectors that save time and improve efficiency.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Profile -->
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="solo-profile fade-up">
        <img src="/images/pallav.jpg" alt="Pallav Rawat" class="team-photo" width="160" height="160" loading="lazy" />
        <div>
          <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/pallav-rawat-9aa50b70" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pallav Rawat</a></h3>
          <span class="team-role">AI Enablement &middot; Stockholm, Sweden</span>
          <p>8+ years across data, tech, and analytics — data strategy, solution development, electrification, and autonomous systems. Co-founded and led Silk Route AB, building Scandinavia's first premium instant chai brand across D2C, Amazon, and retail in Europe, as CEO from Dec 2024 to Aug 2026. Now co-owner, part-time, while Silk Route runs on automated operations with minimal daily involvement.</p>
          <p>Since Aug 2026, focused on Heurystics: finding real AI use cases inside businesses and building the tools that handle them. Open to contract engagements — AI Requirements Engineering, AI Product Manager, AI Forward Deployed Engineer, Data Analyst, Business Analyst — as well as independent consulting.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why -->
  <section class="section section-limestone">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 640px; text-align: center;">
      <div class="editorial fade-up">
        <p>The objective is to become genuinely hands-on with AI — learning by building real, working systems rather than staying theoretical. Every project turns into a case study and a build-in-public track record: an asset that stays useful whichever path opens up next.</p>
        <p>That could be employment as an AI Forward Deployed Engineer or adjacent enablement role, independent consulting work, or eventually building something of my own. The near-term work is the same regardless of destination: build real systems, document them well, and share openly — including what didn't work.</p>
        <p>I don't sell a fixed package. If you've got a process worth automating, I'll tell you honestly whether there's a real use case in it before we talk about building anything.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How I work -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="process-timeline">
        <div class="process-step fade-up">
          <div class="process-circle">
            <span class="process-num mono">01</span>
          </div>
          <div class="process-content">
            <h4>Conversation</h4>
            <p>A short, no-pitch conversation about what's actually eating time. If there's no real use case, I'll say so.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process-line"></div>

        <div class="process-step fade-up delay-1">
          <div class="process-circle">
            <span class="process-num mono">02</span>
          </div>
          <div class="process-content">
            <h4>A tightly scoped build</h4>
            <p>The smallest thing that proves the use case, wired into the tools you already use — not a platform migration.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process-line"></div>

        <div class="process-step fade-up delay-2">
          <div class="process-circle">
            <span class="process-num mono">03</span>
          </div>
          <div class="process-content">
            <h4>Public write-up, your call on what's next</h4>
            <p>What got built, how, and whether it worked — documented as a case study. You decide whether to extend it, keep it, or stop.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABlock />

</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  .solo-profile {
    display: flex;
    gap: 32px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .solo-profile .team-photo {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .team-role {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ochre);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }

  .solo-profile p {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--driftwood);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }

  /* Editorial */
  .editorial p {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75);
  }

  .editorial p + p {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  /* Process timeline */
  .process-timeline {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: stretch;
  }

  .process-step {
    display: flex;
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .process-circle {
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 2px solid var(--limestone);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    background: var(--nordic-light);
  }

  .process-num {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--navy);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .process-content {
    flex: 1;
    padding-top: 12px;
  }

  .process-content h4 {
    font-size: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .process-content p {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--driftwood);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .process-line {
    width: 2px;
    height: 32px;
    background: var(--limestone);
    margin-left: 27px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .solo-profile {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      text-align: center;
    }
  }
</style>
